its_encode_valid(cmd, desc->its_vmapp_cmd.valid);
its_encode_alloc(cmd, alloc);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the code does not properly handle the scenario where a VSYNC command is issued after a VMAPP command that unmapped a Virtual Processing Element (VPE). According to the GICv4.1 specification, the effects of the VMAPP command are not complete until all its effects are finalized. If a VSYNC command is issued in this state, it may reference a non-existent VPE, potentially leading to a system error (SError).

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
vpe = NULL;
goto out;
```
Reason:
The fix involves setting the `vpe` variable to `NULL` when the VPE is unmapped, effectively preventing the issuance of a VSYNC command in this scenario. This change ensures that the VSYNC command is not executed when it would reference an unmapped VPE, thus adhering to the GICv4.1 specification and preventing the potential delivery of an SError.

